        "original_id": "2b99c033-3457-5f83-9978-e786d1525405",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Iqbal F. Qadir\n- Events: Second war with India, attack on the radar station in Dwarka\n- Places: Dwarka, India, Okhamandal Peninsula, Gomti River\n\nFacts:\n- Iqbal F. Qadir is renowned for participating in the second war with India.\n- Iqbal F. Qadir was part of the flotilla that attacked the radar station in Dwarka, India, during the second war with India.\n- Dwarka is located on the western shore of the Okhamandal Peninsula.\n- Dwarka is located on the right bank of the Gomti River.",
